    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/academic-services-officer-port-hedland-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Academic Services Officer",
      "description": "Academic Services Officer - Port Hedland, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Academic Services Officer 524645 Port Hedland, WA Part Time Closing on: 25 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Join a collaborative team committed to enhancing rural health education and improving health outcomes in regional and remote communities. Part-time (0.5 FTE) appointment on a fixed-term basis for 7 months. Base salary range: Level 5: $86,540 - $95,920 p.a. plus 17% superannuation. Must reside in Port Hedland About the area The Rural Clinical School of Western Australia (RCSWA) is part of the UWA Medical School within the Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences. RCSWA delivers high-quality rural clinical education to medical students from The University of Western Australia, Curtin University and The University of Notre Dame Australia. Operating across a network that spans more than 3,500 kilometres throughout Western Australia, RCSWA provides students with meaningful rural clinical experiences while contributing to the development of a skilled rural medical workforce and improved health outcomes for rural and remote communities. The Academic Services team delivers professional administrative and academic support services to staff and students across the School, with a strong focus on service excellence, collaboration and continuous improvement. About the opportunity Coordinate and deliver a broad range of administrative services that support students, academic staff and Medical Coordinators at a designated RCSWA site. Provide high-quality advice, information and support on procedures, processes and operational activities while responding to complex enquiries with initiative and sound judgement. Contribute to continuous improvement by identifying and implementing enhancements to administrative systems, workflows and service delivery practices. About you Relevant tertiary qualification or an equivalent combination of education, training and substantial administrative experience. Demonstrated experience providing high-level administrative support in a complex and customer-focused environment. Strong organisational skills with the ability to manage competing priorities, work independently and meet deadlines. Well-developed written and verbal communication skills, with proven ability to build productive relationships with a diverse range of stakeholders. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications and other business systems, together with a commitment to service excellence and continuous improvement. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. Position description: PD [Academic Services Officer] [524645].pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Robyn Fortune at robyn.fortune@rcswa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Talent Advisor at petrina.gomez@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Sunday, 25 October 2026 This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Please note: Unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 22783f19 Last Name (required) bf29327f Email (required) e135de09 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Senior Brand Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Coordinate and deliver integrated brand campaigns and initiatives across multiple channels, at WA’s top university. Events Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Deliver high-quality events and experiences that strengthen engagement, support strategic priorities and showcase the best of UWA to internal and external audiences. Senior Technician (Safety) Crawley, WA Technical/Laboratory support Be a key driver of safety culture and compliance across diverse research and teaching environments. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 34da5f70 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administration & Executive support Administration & Executive support Employment Type Part Time Part Time Locations Port Hedland, WA, Australia Port Hedland, WA, Australia First Name (required) efaf7301 Last Name (required) 0a6f9476 Email (required) bf9465a5 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
