    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/senior-legal-counsel-crawley-wa-australia-46046b19-c75a-4742-8597-c2618d534285": {
      "title": "Senior Legal Counsel",
      "description": "Senior Legal Counsel - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Senior Legal Counsel 524557 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 25 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Play a pivotal role in providing trusted legal advice that supports the strategic objectives of one of Australia's leading research-intensive universities. Join a collaborative and highly respected legal team advising senior leaders and decision-makers across the University. Full-time appointment on a fixed term basis for 9 months. Competitive salary package including 17% superannuation. About the area The Office of General Counsel plays a critical role within the Office of Vice-Chancellery, providing expert legal advice and strategic support across the University. The team advises on a broad range of legal matters including governance, compliance, contracts, intellectual property, research, commercialisation, procurement, property, risk management and regulatory obligations. Working closely with the University Executive, senior leaders, schools and business units, the Office of General Counsel helps navigate complex legal issues, supports sound decision-making and enables the University to achieve its strategic objectives with confidence. About the opportunity Provide high-quality, pragmatic legal advice across a diverse range of matters including governance, compliance, commercial contracts, research, intellectual property, procurement, property and risk management. Draft, negotiate and advise on complex agreements relating to major projects, strategic education initiatives, research collaborations, commercialisation activities, philanthropy, technology, infrastructure and property transactions. Partner with senior stakeholders across the University, supervise external legal providers when required, and contribute to legal capability through training, guidance and continuous improvement of legal templates and precedents. About you Admitted as a legal practitioner in Western Australia with a current unrestricted practising certificate and at least seven years' post-admission experience. Significant experience providing legal advice in a private practice and/or in-house legal environment, including drafting, reviewing and negotiating complex commercial agreements. Strong stakeholder management skills, with experience advising senior executives and diverse stakeholder groups within large and complex organisations. Exceptional communication, relationship-building and analytical skills, with the ability to translate complex legal issues into practical, business-focused advice. Proven ability to manage competing priorities, exercise sound professional judgement and independently handle complex legal matters to tight deadlines. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. A current National Police Clearance will be required by the successful applicant. Current unrestricted practicing certificate under the Legal Profession Uniform Law (WA). Position description: PD - Senior Legal Counsel 524557.pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact David Nolan at david.nolan@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Pratik Sridhar at pratik.sridhar@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Sunday, 25 October 2026 This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia Please note: Unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 9caebea2 Last Name (required) a23daafc Email (required) 4bd2ab92 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Senior Brand Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Coordinate and deliver integrated brand campaigns and initiatives across multiple channels, at WA’s top university. Academic Services Officer Port Hedland, WA Administration & Executive support Based in Port Hedland I Play a key role in supporting medical students undertaking rural clinical training across Western Australia. Events Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Deliver high-quality events and experiences that strengthen engagement, support strategic priorities and showcase the best of UWA to internal and external audiences. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 5150b6ef Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Executive Executive Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Crawley, WA, Australia First Name (required) 1a51ee4c Last Name (required) e3e7b899 Email (required) 2aadfd77 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essen