    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/senior-strategic-business-officer-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Senior Strategic Business Officer",
      "description": "Senior Strategic Business Officer - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Senior Strategic Business Officer 524547 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 20 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Influence the future development of one of Australia's leading university campuses. Lead campus planning, design and sustainability initiatives with lasting impact. Full-time appointment on an ongoing basis. Base salary range: $108,413 – $120,287 p.a. (pro-rata) plus 17% superannuation. About the area Campus Management is responsible for planning, developing, managing and operating The University of Western Australia’s physical estate and infrastructure. Working within the Estate Strategy team, you will help shape a future-focused, sustainable and inclusive campus environment that supports world-class teaching, research and community engagement. The team leads strategic estate planning, campus master planning, design frameworks and precinct development initiatives, ensuring the University's built, natural and cultural assets continue to support its long-term strategic objectives. Drawing on best practice in urban planning, campus development and stakeholder engagement, the team delivers projects that balance heritage, sustainability, accessibility and innovation. About the opportunity Lead stakeholder engagement across academic, professional and external partners to inform campus master planning, estate strategy, design frameworks and development priorities. Coordinate the delivery and ongoing evolution of UWA's Campus Masterplan, precinct plans, heritage and cultural heritage frameworks, public realm initiatives and place-making programs, working across multidisciplinary technical teams and stakeholders to deliver integrated planning outcomes Provide strategic advice, analysis and governance support across campus development projects, ensuring alignment with sustainability, inclusivity, accessibility, urban design and institutional objectives. About you Degree with at least four years of subsequent relevant work experience, or extensive experience and demonstrated management expertise in a relevant field, or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and/or education/training. Experience in stakeholder management in education or large-scale institutional environments. Knowledge of planning legislation, approvals processes, codes, regulatory and development requirements in Western Australia including statutory planning, urban design, and relevant policy frameworks. Demonstrated ability to engage with diverse stakeholders including executives, government agencies, consultants, community groups, and multidisciplinary technical teams. High level analytical and conceptual skills with the ability to translate vision into practical frameworks and deliverables. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. A current National Police Clearance will be required by the successful applicant. Position description: PD - Senior Strategic Business Officer (524547).pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Melita O'Donnell at melita.odonnell@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Shelby Corrins at shelby.corrins@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume (max. 4 pages) and Cover Letter (max. 2 pages) should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Tuesday, 20 October 2026 This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Please note: Unsolicited applications and emails from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) be0df10b Last Name (required) 88ffc88e Email (required) bcb6cf4f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Senior Brand Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Coordinate and deliver integrated brand campaigns and initiatives across multiple channels, at WA’s top university. Academic Services Officer Port Hedland, WA Administration & Executive support Based in Port Hedland I Play a key role in supporting medical students undertaking rural clinical training across Western Australia. Events Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Deliver high-quality events and experiences that strengthen engagement, support strategic priorities and showcase the best of UWA to internal and external audiences. Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
