    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/development-manager-crawley-wa-australia-c2554433-08cf-4538-b112-fc9febb2a5d6": {
      "title": "Development Manager",
      "description": "Development Manager - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Development Manager 524621 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 2 Nov 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Development Manager (524621) Play a leading role in securing philanthropy that advances world class research, student opportunity, and community impact. Shape and secure major gifts, working closely with senior academic and executive leaders to create compelling philanthropic opportunities. Full-time (1.0 FTE) appointment on an ongoing basis. Base salary range: $120,912 – $132,161 p.a. (pro-rata) plus 17% superannuation. About the area Development and Alumni Relations (DAR) leads the University’s alumni, philanthropic and community engagement strategies. The team works collaboratively across UWA to strengthen donor relationships, secure philanthropic support, and embed engagement activity into the University’s long-term goals. DAR plays a pivotal role in driving the University’s vision by cultivating meaningful partnerships with alumni, corporate partners, charitable foundations, and the wider community. About the opportunity Manage a portfolio of major and prospective donors, securing significant philanthropic gifts of $100,000+ to advance University-wide priorities. Lead tailored fundraising projects, proposals and engagement activities while collaborating with DAR colleagues and cross-campus partners. Support the full donor lifecycle—from identification through to stewardship—ensuring meaningful donor recognition and long-term relationship growth. About you Strong experience managing major gift fundraising programs, ideally within a large or complex not-for-profit environment. Demonstrated success in identifying, cultivating and securing major gifts from high-net-worth donors. Excellent communication and negotiation skills, with the ability to engage sensitively and confidently with diverse stakeholders. Proven ability to work both independently and collaboratively, managing deadlines and contributing to team success. Highly developed interpersonal skills and the ability to build trusted, long-term donor relationships. Sound understanding of philanthropic fundraising in Australia, alongside proficiency in CRM systems and MS Office. Note : Employment checks will include information on gender-based violence, sexual harassment, and related misconduct to meet legal obligations. Position description: Development Manager PD.pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Ingrid Barnard at Ingrid.Barnard@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Zander Ribbens at Zander.Ribbens@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Monday 2nd November. This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Please note: Unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 91fbcec7 Last Name (required) 9a75b38a Email (required) d884b69d Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Senior Brand Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Coordinate and deliver integrated brand campaigns and initiatives across multiple channels, at WA’s top university. Academic Services Officer Port Hedland, WA Administration & Executive support Based in Port Hedland I Play a key role in supporting medical students undertaking rural clinical training across Western Australia. Events Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Deliver high-quality events and experiences that strengthen engagement, support strategic priorities and showcase the best of UWA to internal and external audiences. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 72d4d13e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Community Engagement/Marketing Community Engagement/Marketing Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Crawley, WA, Australia First Name (required) 2bb086ca Last Name (required) 8af5950f Email (required) 88e7fd78 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
