    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/research-technician-animal-research-harry-perkins-institute-of-medical-research-wa-australia-crawley": {
      "title": "Research Technician (Animal Research)",
      "description": "Research Technician (Animal Research) - Harry Perkins Institute of Medical Research, WA, Australia - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Research Technician (Animal Research) 524484 Crawley, WA Harry Perkins Institute of Medical Research, WA Full Time Closing on: 20 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Contribute to innovative cancer research investigating new therapeutic approaches for hard-to-treat cancers. Apply your animal research and laboratory skills in a collaborative research environment at the Harry Perkins Institute of Medical Research. Full-time (1.0 FTE) appointment on a fixed term basis for 12 months. Base salary range: $86,540 – $95,920 p.a. (pro-rata) plus 17% superannuation. About the area The Cancer Epigenetics Laboratory, within the UWA Centre for Medical Research and UWA Medical School, is based at the Harry Perkins Institute of Medical Research in Nedlands. The fully funded laboratory is developing novel therapeutic approaches for hard-to-treat cancers, with research spanning CRISPR-based manipulation of the cancer epigenome and the characterisation of an oncogene involved in cancer resistance to therapy. You will join a collaborative research environment and work alongside a lead research associate and postdoctoral researchers to support these projects, with a particular focus on animal research. About the opportunity Undertake in vivo experimental procedures involving laboratory mice, including animal handling and monitoring, treatment administration, dissections, surgical procedures, tissue collection and sample processing. Support molecular biology and histology workflows, including RNA/DNA extraction, PCR, immunohistochemistry and preparation of biological samples for downstream analysis. Provide day-to-day technical support to cancer research projects, working collaboratively with postdoctoral researchers and research associates. About you A Science degree; or a diploma with at least two years' relevant animal handling experience; or an equivalent combination of relevant education, training and experience. Strong practical experience in animal handling, sample processing and the use of laboratory equipment. Effective written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to contribute positively within a collaborative research team. Strong organisational skills, with the ability to prioritise competing activities and meet deadlines. Proficiency using standard workplace technology, including word processing, spreadsheets and email. Note : Employment checks will include information on gender-based violence, sexual harassment, and related misconduct to meet legal obligations. A current National Police Clearance, and “C” class driver’s licence will be required by the successful applicant. Position description: Research Technician (Animal Research) PD.pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Chee Wai Wong at chee.wong@perkins.org.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Zander Ribbens at Zander.Ribbens@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Tuesday 20th October. The university reserves the right to close advertising early if required. This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Please note: Unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) e4a1c86c Last Name (required) 8393642a Email (required) 8f75d60e Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Senior Brand Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Coordinate and deliver integrated brand campaigns and initiatives across multiple channels, at WA’s top university. Academic Services Officer Port Hedland, WA Administration & Executive support Based in Port Hedland I Play a key role in supporting medical students undertaking rural clinical training across Western Australia. Events Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Deliver high-quality events and experiences that strengthen engagement, support strategic priorities and showcase the best of UWA to internal and external audiences. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 8face7b7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Research support Research support Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Harry Perkins Institute of Medical Research, WA, Australia Crawley, WA, Australia Harry Perkins Institute of Medical Research, WA, Australia First Name (required) ddb78bde Last Name (required) c198c7f8 Email (required) 1cebf425 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
