    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/casual-internship-adviser-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Casual",
      "description": "Casual – Internship Adviser - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Casual – Internship Adviser 523337 Crawley, WA Casual Closing on: 1 Nov 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Support a high-impact internship program making a difference in communities. Collaborate with students and partners to foster active citizenship. Casual appointment Base salary range: $50.63 - $53.51 per hour (plus 25% casual loading) plus superannuation The work area The McCusker Centre for Citizenship (The Centre) was established in late 2015. The Centre is collaborating with students and the broader UWA community, not for profit and community organisations, industry, government and business to make a difference in our communities locally, nationally and globally. The McCusker Centre for Citizenship offers an award winning structured, quality internship program with not for profit, community and government organisations locally, regionally and globally About the opportunity Support the delivery and efficient operation of the internship program through high-level coordination, administration, and stakeholder engagement. Act as one of the main contacts for students and partners, providing quality advice and resolving issues to ensure positive outcomes. Collaborate with other internship advisers and become part of a Team during busy periods. About you Relevant tertiary qualifications in a relevant discipline or equivalent competency. Experience in working closely with students, student systems and industry partners to deliver a quality program. Highly developed organisational skills and demonstrated ability to set priorities and to meet deadlines and deliver on specific outcomes. Ability to critically analyse and problem solve to identify service improvements and efficiencies. Proficiency in a range of computing skills in word processing, spreadsheets and project plans, databases, internet, email and website development. 