    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/lead-engineer-optical-systems-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Lead Engineer, Optical Systems",
      "description": "Lead Engineer, Optical Systems - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Lead Engineer, Optical Systems 524703 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 1 Nov 2026 Lead the optical and optomechanical engineering effort across a portfolio of externally funded programs in free-space optical communications, satellite laser ranging and ground-to-space optical terminals. Join a cutting-edge research group developing advanced photonic systems for astronomy, space science, quantum technologies and national security. Full-time appointment on a fixed term basis until 31/12/2027 Base salary: Level 8, $120,912 – 132,161 p.a. plus 17% superannuation. About the area The International Centre for Radio Astronomy Research (ICRAR) is a joint venture between Curtin University and The University of Western Australia (UWA), established in 2009 and funded through 2030 with $65 million from the WA State Government. ICRAR is a leading institution in radio astronomy and a key Australian contributor to the global SKA project. The Astrophotonics Group within ICRAR develops advanced photonic systems for radio and optical astronomy, with a focus on long-distance transfer of stabilised frequency and timing signals via optical fibre and free-space laser links. About the opportunity Act as ICRAR’s technical authority on free-space optical and optomechanical systems, setting the technical requirements, design standards and verification approaches for optical systems across the Astrophotonics group. Manage delivery of the optical engineering work packages across concurrent programs, including technical priorities, schedules and equipment budgets, and direct and mentor engineers, technical officers, research staff and postgraduate students. Represent ICRAR in design reviews and technical exchanges with industry, defence and government partners, and lead laboratory, field and on-platform integration and test campaigns, including deployments to remote observatory sites and to maritime and airborne platforms. About you A postgraduate qualification in optical science and engineering, photonics, physics or a related discipline, with extensive experience and demonstrated standing as an authority in optical and optomechanical system design. Demonstrated expertise in the design, fabrication, alignment and testing of free-space optical terminals, including single-mode fibre coupling, multi-wavelength beam co-alignment and precision optomechanical mounting, using tools such as Zemax OpticStudio and 3D CAD. Experience with telescope and optical ground station systems, including pointing, acquisition and tracking, high-power laser installation, and laser safety requirements. Demonstrated technical leadership and mentoring of engineering staff and students, and experience advising and negotiating technical requirements with industry, defence and government partners and delivering against contracted milestones. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. Position description: Lead Engineer, Optical Systems - 524703 To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Sascha Schediwy at sascha.schediwy@uwa.edu.au For any recruitment related queries please contact Zen Huang at zen.huang@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Sunday, 01 November 2026 This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia Please note: Unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. Alternatively, please contact the Talent team at people@uwa.edu.au with details of your query. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 0bce3684 Last Name (required) 53ae43da Email (required) c87469c8 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Ethics Officer Crawley, WA Research support Help enable responsible, high-quality research by supporting robust ethics review, governance and committee processes. Senior Brand Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Coordinate and deliver integrated brand campaigns and initiatives across multiple channels, at WA’s top university. Academic Services Officer Port Hedland, WA Administration & Executive support Based in Port Hedland I Play a key role in supporting medical students undertaking rural clinical training across Western Australia. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 92b69462 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Research support Research support Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Crawley, WA, Australia First Name (required) 0522756e Last Name (required) 2daadad2 Email (required) be1ee2db Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
