    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/senior-program-accountant-eerp-claremont-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Senior Program Accountant (EERP)",
      "description": "Senior Program Accountant (EERP) - Claremont, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Senior Program Accountant (EERP) 523583 Claremont, WA Full Time Closing on: 25 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Join a university-wide remediation program with significant organisational impact. Lead financial governance, compliance and continuous improvement initiatives. Full-time appointment on a fixed term basis until December 2027 with potential to extend. Base salary range: $120,912 – $132,161 p.a. plus 17% superannuation. About the area The Employee Entitlements Remediation Program (EERP) at UWA addresses historical and ongoing payroll compliance issues, ensuring accurate and fair compensation of employees in alignment with legislative requirements, including the Fair Work Act 2009, relevant Enterprise Agreements, and statutory instruments. About the opportunity Manage and oversee financial planning, budgeting, forecasting, and reporting for programs and projects. Provide informed, strategic advice to the EERP leadership on financial impacts and risks related to entitlement remediation and budgets. Identify, recommend, and implement process improvements to enhance efficiency, effectiveness, and compliance of EERP financial activities. About you Relevant tertiary qualification in Accounting, Finance, or related business discipline or equivalent demonstrated competency. Full professional membership of a recognised Australian or International accounting body (CPA, CA, or equivalent). Demonstrated experience in payroll compliance, data analytics, and accounting within complex organisational settings, ideally within higher education or similarly complex environments. Extensive knowledge of Australian Accounting Standards, payroll legislation, Fair Work Act compliance, and external audit requirements. Proven analytical and problem-solving skills with exceptional attention to detail and ability to manage large datasets and complex financial scenarios. Note : Employment checks will include information on gender-based violence, sexual harassment, and related misconduct to meet legal obligations. A current National Police Clearance and Finance Checks will be required by the successful applicant. Position description: PD - Senior Program Accountant (EERP) 523583.pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Dana Prybysh at dana.prybysh@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Pratik Sridhar at pratik.sridhar@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Sunday, 25 October 2026 This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia, Candidates may be interviewed prior to the application end date based on their suitability for the position, you are therefore encouraged to apply at your earliest convenience Please note: Unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. Alternatively, please contact the Talent team at people@uwa.edu.au with details of your query. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 96c51fe2 Last Name (required) e0b6eb9b Email (required) 3d236111 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Lead Engineer, Optical Systems Crawley, WA Research support Lead optical systems engineering across space communications, laser ranging and photonics programs with UWA's internationally recognised ICRAR team Ethics Officer Crawley, WA Research support Help enable responsible, high-quality research by supporting robust ethics review, governance and committee processes. Senior Brand Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Coordinate and deliver integrated brand campaigns and initiatives across multiple channels, at WA’s top university. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 93cdc054 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Finance Finance Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Claremont, WA, Australia Claremont, WA, Australia First Name (required) 5afb99e3 Last Name (required) 86ed4193 Email (required) 926deccb Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
