    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/pro-vice-chancellor-research-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Pro Vice-Chancellor (Research)",
      "description": "Pro Vice-Chancellor (Research) - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Pro Vice-Chancellor (Research) 524745 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 22 Nov 2026 Provide strategic leadership across research institutes, international research and major research infrastructure investment. A senior management position on a five-year fixed-term contract, with the possibility of renewal. Secondment arrangements are strongly encouraged and will be actively considered. About the area The Office of the Deputy Vice-Chancellor (Research) provides strategic leadership for research across The University of Western Australia. Working across Schools, research institutes, professional portfolios and external partners, the portfolio advances research excellence, capability, collaboration and impact. The portfolio oversees research strategy, policy and operations, including postgraduate research education, research quality and performance, research ethics and integrity, research infrastructure, industry engagement, commercialisation, international research and UWA's Strategic Research Institutes. Reporting to the Deputy Vice-Chancellor (Research), the Pro Vice-Chancellor (Research) is a key member of UWA's senior academic leadership team. The role works closely with academic and professional leaders across the University to strengthen research performance, build institutional capability, foster collaboration, and ensure strategic investment supports areas of research strength and emerging opportunity. About the opportunity Provide strategic leadership across designated research institutes and entities, research infrastructure, international research and institution-wide research capability initiatives. Shape and steward UWA's research infrastructure portfolio, driving investment, sustainability, research partnerships, multidisciplinary collaboration and research impact. Build and maintain influential relationships with government, industry, funders, universities and research organisations to enhance UWA's research reputation, performance and global engagement. About you A doctoral qualification and academic standing at Professorial level (Level E or equivalent), supported by a distinguished international research profile. Demonstrated success leading complex research portfolios, multidisciplinary institutes, major research collaborations or comparable research-intensive organisations. Proven expertise in research strategy, governance, infrastructure investment, organisational performance and translating strategic priorities into measurable outcomes. Strong ability to develop research leaders, strengthen research culture and build capability across disciplines, schools and institutional boundaries. Exceptional stakeholder engagement, influencing and partnership-building skills, with experience working effectively across government, industry, funding bodies and international research networks Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. Candidate Information Booklet: Candidate Information Booklet - Pro Vice-Chancellor (Research).pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Professor Anna Nowak at anna.nowak@uwa.edu.au and/or Professor Andrew Page at andrew.page@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Talent Advisor at petrina.gomez@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. Applications should include a statement addressing the selection criteria, a current Curriculum Vitae, and, where relevant, an optional one-page statement outlining any personal circumstances or career interruptions to support consideration of achievements relative to opportunity. Recruitment Process and Key Dates •  Selection activities may include Microsoft Teams interviews and/or in-person interviews. •  Shortlisted candidates should be available to attend interviews on Monday, 30 November 2026 and Friday, 4 December 2026. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Monday, 23 November 2026 This position is open to international applicants. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Other jobs Casuals (UWA Law School) – Expression of Interest Crawley, WA Law Engage in various casual activities, such as tutoring and marking, at the The University of Western Australia's Law School. Lecturer (Statistics) Crawley, WA Engineering and Mathematical Sciences Build your academic career within a highly regarded department known for excellence in research, industry collaboration and student outcomes Executive Assistant & Project Officer Crawley, WA Administration & Executive support Provide executive support and project coordination to the Director, Student Living, helping deliver strategic initiatives and student success. Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/dental-clinic-assistants-oral-health-centre-of-wa-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Dental Clinic Assistants",
      "description": "Dental Clinic Assistants - Oral Health Centre of WA, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Dental Clinic Assistants 524797 Oral Health Centre of WA, WA Casual Closing on: 6 Nov 2026 UWA Dental School Join a state-of-the-art dental teaching and learning facility Casual appointment Base salary range: $34.25 – $37.93 per hour (plus 25% casual loading) plus 12% superannuation About the opportunity Are you passionate about patient care and looking for flexible work in a dynamic clinical environment? We are seeking Dental Clinic Assistants to support our team in delivering high quality dental care. Provide clinical assistance to dental students and OHCWA clinical staff during patient treatment Maintain high standards of infection control and hygiene throughout the clinic Provide excellent patient care and ensure a safe and welcoming environment, and conduct administrative duties as required within the clinic About you Completion of Certificate III or Certificate IV in Dental Clinic Assisting or equivalent. Current knowledge of dental assisting procedures and experience in dental assistance within public dental or teaching facilities. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills Strong organisational skills, with the ability to prioritise tasks Note: A current first aid certificate and working with children check will be required by the successful applicant. To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Lina Brunini at lina.brunini@uwa.edu.au Applications will be retained on our casual register for 12 months. Should an opportunity arise matching your skills and experience, you will be contacted by the relevant work area. This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Application Details: Please apply online via the Apply Now button. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. Back to job search Other jobs Casuals (UWA Law School) – Expression of Interest Crawley, WA Law Engage in various casual activities, such as tutoring and marking, at the The University of Western Australia's Law School. Lecturer (Statistics) Crawley, WA Engineering and Mathematical Sciences Build your academic career within a highly regarded department known for excellence in research, industry collaboration and student outcomes Executive Assistant & Project Officer Crawley, WA Administration & Executive support Provide executive support and project coordination to the Director, Student Living, helping deliver strategic initiatives and student success. Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
