    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/category-manager-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Category Manager",
      "description": "Category Manager - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Category Manager 524295 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 4 Nov 2026 Lead strategic procurement and category management at one of Australia's leading research-intensive universities. Develop and deliver against category strategies that achieve value for money, mitigate supply and commercial risks, and support sustainable procurement outcomes across the University. Full-time (1 FTE) appointment on a fixed term basis for 12 months. Base salary range: Level 9, $139,660 – $147,783 p.a. plus 17% superannuation. About the area Finance supports the University through the delivery of strategic financial advice, governance, procurement, financial performance, compliance, and operational services. The Procurement team partners with stakeholders across the University to deliver value-driven sourcing solutions, optimise expenditure, strengthen supplier relationships, and support the University's strategic objectives. As part of this function, the Procurement team works with academic and professional areas across the University to ensure best-practice procurement, commercial risk management, sustainable sourcing, and effective contract management. About the opportunity Lead the development and execution of category management strategies, strategic sourcing initiatives, and procurement plans that maximise value, support sustainability objectives, and strengthen supply chain resilience. Provide expert commercial advice on procurement, contract negotiation, supplier performance, risk management, contract and supplier management and value optimisation while partnering with stakeholders across the University. Lead and develop a high-performing procurement team, driving continuous improvement, capability uplift, compliance, and best-practice procurement outcomes. About you Relevant postgraduate qualification, MCIPS accreditation, or equivalent demonstrated procurement and commercial expertise. Extensive experience in category management, strategic sourcing, contract management, supplier relationship management, and procurement across diverse spend categories. Proven leadership experience with the ability to manage teams, resources, projects, and organisational priorities in a complex environment. Strong commercial and analytical capability, with demonstrated success negotiating complex commercial agreements and delivering measurable value outcomes. Exceptional stakeholder engagement, communication, presentation, and influencing skills, with the ability to provide trusted advice and procurement training to diverse audiences. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. A current National Police Clearance will be required by the successful applicant. Position description: Category Manager - 524295.pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Emma Gillespie at emma.gillespie@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Zen Huang at zen.huang@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Wednesday, 04 November 2026. The University reserves the right to interview and appoint a suitably qualified candidate prior to the closing date. This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia Please note: Unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Other jobs Casuals (UWA Law School) – Expression of Interest Crawley, WA Law Engage in various casual activities, such as tutoring and marking, at the The University of Western Australia's Law School. Lecturer (Statistics) Crawley, WA Engineering and Mathematical Sciences Build your academic career within a highly regarded department known for excellence in research, industry collaboration and student outcomes Executive Assistant & Project Officer Crawley, WA Administration & Executive support Provide executive support and project coordination to the Director, Student Living, helping deliver strategic initiatives and student success. Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/executive-officer-crawley-wa-australia-91d85f6c-491b-44af-962d-3776357a41db": {
      "title": "Executive Officer",
      "description": "Executive Officer - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Executive Officer 524750 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 3 Nov 2026 Shape financial strategy and governance across the University, working directly with the Chief Financial Officer. Lead high-impact portfolio coordination, strategic advice and stakeholder engagement in a complex university environment. Full-time (1.0 FTE) appointment on an ongoing basis. Base salary range: $139,660 – $147,783 p.a. (pro-rata) plus 17% superannuation. About the area The Chief Financial Officer (CFO) Portfolio leads the University's financial strategy, policy and compliance across financial planning and budget, financial administration, management and reporting, procurement, and investment and debt strategies. Finance delivers this work through three core pillars: Financial Compliance, Financial Performance and Procurement, partnering across the University to advise senior leaders on strategy, governance and performance. About the opportunity Project manage the delivery of University-wide financial strategy and supporting governance frameworks, policies and processes. Coordinate CFO Portfolio priorities and deliverables across multiple internal and external stakeholders, providing timely strategic analysis, advice and executive support to the CFO. Strengthen financial governance by overseeing audit-related portfolio activity, supporting senior committees and working groups, and driving continuous improvement in governance processes. About you Relevant tertiary qualifications or demonstrated equivalent experience, together with substantial corporate and financial governance experience at an appropriate level. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the judgement to prepare strategic advice, reports and recommendations on complex or sensitive matters. Strong project management, planning and organisational capability, including the ability to set priorities, meet deadlines and coordinate contributions from multiple stakeholders. Demonstrated ability to build productive stakeholder relationships, work independently, use initiative and deliver customer-focused outcomes in a complex environment. Excellent analytical and digital capability, including experience interrogating data and developing dashboards and business reports using contemporary office, spreadsheet and database tools. Note : Employment checks will include information on gender-based violence, sexual harassment, and related misconduct to meet legal obligations. A current National Police Clearance will be required by the successful applicant. Position description: Executive Officer PD.PDF For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Zander Ribbens at Zander.Ribbens@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Tuesday 3rd November This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Please note: Unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Other jobs Casuals (UWA Law School) – Expression of Interest Crawley, WA Law Engage in various casual activities, such as tutoring and marking, at the The University of Western Australia's Law School. Lecturer (Statistics) Crawley, WA Engineering and Mathematical Sciences Build your academic career within a highly regarded department known for excellence in research, industry collaboration and student outcomes Executive Assistant & Project Officer Crawley, WA Administration & Executive support Provide executive support and project coordination to the Director, Student Living, helping deliver strategic initiatives and student success. Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
